======================================================================
PART D: H(T_p) / |Aut(T_p)| DEEP ANALYSIS
======================================================================

  p=3: H=3, |Aut|=3, H/|Aut|=1
    H factored: 3
    |Aut| factored: 3
    H/|Aut| factored: 1

  p=7: H=189, |Aut|=21, H/|Aut|=9
    H factored: 3 * 3 * 3 * 7
    |Aut| factored: 3 * 7
    H/|Aut| factored: 3 * 3

  p=11: H=95095, |Aut|=55, H/|Aut|=1729
    H factored: 5 * 7 * 11 * 13 * 19
    |Aut| factored: 5 * 11
    H/|Aut| factored: 7 * 13 * 19

  p=19: H=1172695746915, |Aut|=171, H/|Aut|=6857869865
    H factored: 3 * 3 * 5 * 7 * 11 * 19 * 23 * 774463
    |Aut| factored: 3 * 3 * 19
    H/|Aut| factored: 5 * 7 * 11 * 23 * 774463

  --- Arithmetic patterns ---

  p=3:
    |Aut| = 3, p*(p-1)/2 = 3, match: True
    H/(p!) = 5.000000e-01
    H / (p!/2^(p-1)) = 2.000000
    H = sum 2^k * alpha_k (by OCF)

  p=7:
    |Aut| = 21, p*(p-1)/2 = 21, match: True
    H/(p!) = 3.750000e-02
    H / (p!/2^(p-1)) = 2.400000
    H = sum 2^k * alpha_k (by OCF)

  p=11:
    |Aut| = 55, p*(p-1)/2 = 55, match: True
    H/(p!) = 2.382330e-03
    H / (p!/2^(p-1)) = 2.439506
    H = sum 2^k * alpha_k (by OCF)

  p=19:
    |Aut| = 171, p*(p-1)/2 = 171, match: True
    H/(p!) = 9.640304e-06
    H / (p!/2^(p-1)) = 2.527148
    H = sum 2^k * alpha_k (by OCF)

  1729 = 12^3 + 1^3 = 1729
  1729 = 10^3 + 9^3 = 1729
  1729 = 7 * 13 * 19 = 1729
  These primes are: p, p+2, p+6 for p=7? No, p=7 and we need mod structure.
  7 = (p-4)/1, 13 = (p+2)/1, 19 = (p+8)/1 for p=11
  Or: 7*13*19 = C(20,3) - 11? No, C(20,3) = 1140
  Actually: p=11, primes 7,13,19 are p-4, p+2, p+8 = 2k-1 for k=4,7,10 (AP!)
  Arithmetic progression: 4, 7, 10 (common diff 3 = (p-2)/3)

  H/|Aut| for p=19: 6857869865 = 5 * 7 * 11 * 23 * 774463
  Unique primes: [5, 7, 11, 23, 774463]
  Differences from p=19: [-14, -12, -8, 4, 774444]
  Differences from each other: [2, 4, 12, 774440]

